Title:   The Arecibo Legacy Fast ALFA Survey: The ALFALFA Extragalactic HI
         Source Catalog
Authors: Haynes M.P., Giovanelli R., Kent B.R., Adams E.A.K., Balonek T.J., 
         Craig D.W., Fertig, D., Finn, R., Giovanardi, C., Hallenbeck G., 
         Hess K.M., Hoffman G.L., Huang S., Jones, M.G., Koopmann R.A., 
         Kornreich D.A., Leisman, L., Miller J.R., Moorman, C., 
         O'Connor, J., O'Donoghue A.A., Papastergis E., Troischt P., 
         Stark, D., Xiao, L.
Table:   ALFALFA Extragalactic HI Source Catalog
================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file: datafile.table2.txt
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units     Label    Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1-  6 I6     ---       AGCNr    Entry number in catalog
   8- 15 A8     ---       Name     Common name
  17- 31 A15    ---       PosHI    Position (J2000) of HI centroid (1)
  33- 47 A15    ---       PosOC    Position (J2000) of optical counterpart, 
                                    where applicable (1)
  49- 53 I5     km/s      Vhelio   Heliocentric velocity of the HI profile 
                                    midpoint
  55- 57 I3     km/s      W50      Observed velocity width at 50% of peak 
                                    on either side
  59- 61 I3     km/s      sigW50   Uncertainty in W50 
  59- 61 I3     km/s      W20      Observed velocity width at 20% of peak 
                                    on either side
  64- 70 F7.2   Jy.km/s   HIflux   HI line flux density
  72- 75 F4.2   Jy.km/s   sigflux  Uncertainty in HIflux
  78- 82 F5.1   ---       SNR      Ratio of peak flux to rms noise
  85- 89 F5.2   mJy       RMS      The RMS noise in the extracted spectrum 
                                    at 10 km/s resolution
  91- 95 F5.1   Mpc       Dist     Adopted distance, where applicable
         F4.1   Mpc       sigD     Uncertainty in distance, where applicable
  97-101 F5.2   [solMass] logMHI   HI mass in logarithmic solar units, 
                                    where distance has been adopted   
         F4.1   [solMass] siglMHI  Uncertainty in logMHI
     103 I1     ---       HIcode   HI source code (2) 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (1): In hhmmss.s+ddmmss
Note (2): 
      1 = Source of significant S/N and high quality insuring reliability.
      2 = Source of slightly lower S/N which coincides with an optical 
          counterpart of known, coincident redshift.

